 winner even  though i  fell every so often but i always got up  and i always move  forward so remember never think  small think big  [Music]  and the next thing the third point that  i'm gonna make to you is  don't listen to the naysayers  don't listen to the naysayers  everything i ever did the thing that  they heard out of people's mouth was  that's impossible that can't be done  you can't be a bodybuilding champion  that is exactly what i heard and of  course i proved to the people that it  can't be done  [Music]  so whenever someone said to me it can't  be done i heard  it can be done when they said no i heard  yes  and when they said it's impossible i  heard it is possible  if i would have listened to the  naysayers from bodybuilding to show  business to the  to politics i would not be standing here  today  talking to you i will be in austria in  the alps yodeling  that's right i will be in austria still  left yodling  that's what i will be doing exactly  so this is why i say don't listen to the  naysayers  [Music]  my fourth rule is work your ass off  nobody ever stumbled upon success by  accident i always believed  no stone unturned work your butt off  that's what i always believe no matter  what you do  work work work it doesn't matter in what  area you're in  no pain no gain the bottom line is  one of my rules which is work your butt  off  if you don't apply that rule all the  other rules won't mean anything  i believe of what ted turner said who is  one of the great entrepreneurs who  started cnn and so on  he said early to bed early to rise  work like hell and advertise so that's  what i believe  just remember you can climb that ladder  of success  with your hands in your pockets you must  work your ass off it's that simple  [Music]  my fifth and last rule is don't just  take give something back  leave your mark on the world i believe  that we all have an obligation to do  something for our community  something for our state something for  our country  we must serve a cause that is greater  than ourselves  because we all know that on the end we  will be judged  not by how much we made but how much we  give  every single time i reached out and i  gave something back i felt fantastic  nothing made me happier i would rather  play chess with an eight-year-old kid in  an after-school program  or play golf a round of golf with a  special olympian  then go down another red carpet of a  movie premiere and have nothing against  movies  but to give something back to me is more  important than just to think about  myself  so i feel very strongly all of us need  to have  and embrace that kind of a spirit  we all can create change whether it is  in our neighborhood  or in our local schools or in our  country it can be big but it can also be  as little as just going to a school kid  that has problems reading and teaching  that kids how to read  or how to do math we don't have to just  work on  me we should also work on we  not just me but also we remember that  to lead a truly full life you must give  back  you must leave the world a better place  than you found it  [Music]  you
 

